          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"welcome-to-the-google-adk-workshop\">\ud83e\udd16 Welcome to the Google ADK Workshop</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">In this interactive workshop, we're building <strong>Production-Ready Intelligent Agents</strong> natively on Vertex AI using the <strong>Google Agent Development Kit (ADK)</strong>.</span>\n<h3 id=\"system-terminology\">\ud83d\udd11 System Terminology</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Agent</strong>: The core LLM-powered entity. Configured with a <code>model</code>, an <code>instruction</code> prompt, and <code>tools</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Tool</strong>: Standard Python functions (or endpoints) that let Agents execute real-world actions.</li>\n<li><strong>Session</strong>: The stateful memory structure that persists your agent's context across conversation turns.</li>\n<li><strong>Event Stream</strong>: The real-time deterministic output generated by agents (think <code>content</code> chunks, <code>tool_call</code> requests, and <code>grounding_metadata</code>).</li>\n</ul></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "vblA",
      "code_hash": "42d5f03a524c68ffa4dcf8df11523a74",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><hr />\n<h1 id=\"module-01-foundation\">Module 01: Foundation</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The defining building block of the ADK is the <code>Agent</code> class.\nYou define the AI's persona, its capabilities, and let it run.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Hit <strong>Run</strong> on the cell below to securely execute our first ADK Agent right here in the browser!</span></span>"
          }
        }
